The four prior findings are fixed for their reported cases. Three high-severity blockers remain:

- **R10-N30 — Symlink traversal is cleaned before inspection**, at [validate_carry.go:313](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-695147164/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:313). With `unowned/link -> ../other/deep`, a declared dependency `unowned/link/../input` resolves physically to `other/input`. The guards and selection instead use `unowned/input`. A change to `other/input` can therefore leave a self-contained consumer carrying a stale pass. Reject ambiguous traversal or establish physical path identity before cleaning. Established by source tracing, an in-memory selection probe, and a read-only OS path-resolution probe; no new Git fixture was created.
- **R10-N31 — `material_clean` trusts status-hidden edits**, at [validate.go:1435](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-695147164/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1435). Both cleanliness helpers rely on `git status`, which hides edits marked `assume-unchanged` or `skip-worktree`. A baseline can pass over a hidden uncommitted fix, record `material_clean: true`, then supply a stale carried pass after the committed failing content is restored. The existing snapshot regressions demonstrate this status blind spot and passed. Use content-based comparison with the recorded commit.
- **R10-N32 — Unicode filename aliases evade the case guards**, at [validate_carry.go:496](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-695147164/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:496). On case-sensitive APFS, `shared/café.txt` and its decomposed spelling resolve to the same file. A consumer declaring one spelling can miss a change reported under the other. Case swapping does not detect this. Apple documents normalization insensitivity for case-sensitive APFS. This finding is based on source analysis and documented platform behavior, not an APFS fixture run. [Apple APFS FAQ](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/APFS_Guide/FAQ/FAQ.html)

